   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia is supporting drafting of practical tools and step-by-step guidance to uplift public service capability of Pacific countries. In May 2025, APSC hosted 22 senior Human Resource practitioners from across 10 Pacific countries for the Workforce Planning Intensive Workshop in Canberra. Cofacilitated by the Samoan Public Service Commission (PSC), the workshop provided a platform for knowledge exchange and collaboration, and Pacific delegates gained deeper insights into workforce planning challenges and opportunities across the Pacific. Key topics were- workforce data, risk management, succession planning, job design, and implementation strategies. These discussions built on momentum from the 2024 Workforce Planning Study Tour and the 2023 Pacific Public Service Commissioners&#x2019; conference. A major outcome was the co-development of a draft Pacific Public Service Workforce Planning Guideline, led by the Samoan PSC. In addition to supporting practical guidance and tools, the initiative also reinforced Australia&#x2019;s position as a trusted partner in supporting governance reform in the region. Participants were committed to sustaining a Pacific Workforce Planning Community of Practice and recognised that its success relies on continued collaboration, shared experience, and regional engagement.</narrative>
    </description>
